---
import './memory.css';
---
<figure class="memory-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 2</span>The value is only part of the bill</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <p><strong>One illustrative entry: 1,024 bytes (1 KiB)</strong></p>
  <div class="byte-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="value"></span><span class="key"></span><span class="overhead"></span><span class="rounding"></span></div>
  <dl class="byte-parts"><div><dt>Encoded value</dt><dd>900 B</dd></div><div><dt>Key text</dt><dd>29 B</dd></div><div><dt>Bookkeeping</dt><dd>71 B</dd></div><div><dt>Unused allocation</dt><dd>24 B</dd></div></dl>
  <p class="key-text"><code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP</code></p>
  <div class="budget"><strong>Host or container allowance</strong><div class="process"><strong>Cache process</strong><div class="entries"><strong>Entry allocations</strong><div class="cards"><span>P7 · 1 KiB</span><span>P3 · 1 KiB</span><span>P8 · 1 KiB</span></div><div class="large">Or one Q result · 3 KiB</div></div><p>Also: connections, temporary work, retained allocator pages, replication and persistence activity when enabled.</p></div><p>Also: other processes, operating-system needs and room for peaks.</p></div>
  <p class="callout">Three entries can use the same space as one. Neither count tells you the process’s peak resident memory.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>A byte model, not a Redis measurement. The bar is proportional; the exact key is 29 UTF-8 bytes. All other entry sizes are invented. The outer boxes show what belongs in the budget, not proportional memory amounts. Q is a larger catalogue-list result, defined in Figure 4.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
 .byte-bar { display:flex;height:2rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
 .value { width:87.890625%;background:var(--color-accent); }
 .key { width:2.83203125%;background:var(--color-text); }
 .overhead { width:6.93359375%;background:var(--color-text-secondary); }
 .rounding { width:2.34375%;background:var(--color-surface); }
 .byte-parts { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem;margin:1rem 0; }
 .byte-parts dd { margin:0;font-weight:600; }
 .key-text { overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
 .budget,.process,.entries { padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);margin-top:1rem; }
 .budget { border-style:dashed; }.process { background:var(--color-surface); }.entries { border:2px solid var(--color-accent); }
 .cards { display:flex;gap:.35rem;margin-top:.5rem; }.cards span { flex:1;padding:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
 .large { margin-top:.4rem;border:1px dashed var(--color-rule-strong);padding:.5rem; }
 @media(max-width:540px){.byte-parts{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));}.budget,.process,.entries{padding:.55rem;}.cards{flex-direction:column;}}
</style>
